WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.270
[Music] Hold on to your hats. Our narrator, Nick Carraway, has some hair raising things to share about life and love in the

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:19.830
1920s. Was it the roaring 20s or the rotten 20s? You'll have to stick around to find out. Old sport. Nick's an honest kind of

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:28.950
guy who people tend to confide in, which is why he has lots to tell us about what happened in 1922.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:40.150
Of all the people Nick met that year, the one who made the biggest impression on him was Gatsby. Ah, Gatsby.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:48.950
It all began in the summer. Nick had recently moved from America's Midwest to take a job in New York City. He'd also

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:57.750
rented a cottage on Long Island's West Egg, right next door to Gatsby's mansion. Nick's second cousin, Daisy

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:07.190
Buchanan, lived across the bay in the more fashionable East Egg, where the old money resides.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:16.630
One evening, Daisy invites Nick over for dinner. Nick receives a warm welcome from Daisy, but her friend Jordan Baker

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:24.149
is standoffish. Although Jordan does know who Nick's neighbor is, who's Gatsby?

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:33.910
Nick went to Yale with Daisy's obnoxious husband, Tom Buchanan. The unhappy state of Tom and Daisy's marriage is showcased

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:43.030
during dinner when Tom's mistress calls twice. Poor Daisy is clearly miserable.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:51.350
When he arrives back home, Nick sees his neighbor Gatsby standing out on his manicured lawn in the moonlight. Gatsby

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:59.109
holds his arms out towards a green light that flashes in the distance. What's he doing?

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:08.070
A short time later, Tom introduces Nick to his mistress, Myrtle Wilson. She lives in the Valley of the Ashes, an

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:13.589
industrial wasteland that lies halfway between the eggs and New York City.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:17.510
She's married to George Wilson, who owns a garage.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:26.150
George doesn't realize that Tom visits his garage to see Myrtle, not discuss cars. Later that afternoon, they all end

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:37.030
up at Tom and Myrtle's love nest in the city. Myrtle invites a few people over and it turns into a party, but the shindig ends abruptly when Tom breaks

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:43.750
Myrtle's nose for repeating Daisy's name. What a brute.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:49.830
But that wasn't a proper party. Only Gatsby throws real parties.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:58.070
Soon enough, Nick is formally invited to one. Jordan Baker saves him from social isolation, and they go on a mission to

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:08.390
find the mysterious Gatsby. Inside, they find an owly man in the library, but no Gatsby.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:16.550
At around midnight, Gatsby finally introduces himself to Nick. They chat briefly before Gatsby takes a phone call

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.990
and then asks to speak to Jordan alone.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.430
Is Gatsby trying to steal Nick's date?

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:35.270
It turns out that Gatsby had pulled Jordan aside to tell her something amazing. But Nick must make a date with her if he wants to know more. So Nick

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:43.110
starts dating Jordan, even though he hasn't officially broken up with his girlfriend back home.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:52.229
One morning, Gatsby drives Nick into the city in his big yellow car. On the way, Gatsby tells Nick his life story.

00:03:52.239 --> 00:04:00.390
Apparently, he comes from a wealthy Midwest family, is a decorated war hero, was educated at Oxford, and was affected

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:09.509
by a very sad thing that happened in his past. It all sounds like a lie until he pulls out a medal and photo to

00:04:09.519 --> 00:04:19.349
corroborate it. Gatsby also says that Jordan will fill Nick in on the very sad thing. Ah, so that's what Jordan and

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:22.629
Gatsby were discussing at the party.

00:04:22.639 --> 00:04:26.790
Maybe Gatsby is legit.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:36.230
At lunch, Gatsby introduces Nick to his longtime business partner, Meyer Wolfsheim. Bit of a shady character that one.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:47.110
An awkward moment also occurs when Nick bumps into Tom Buchanan at the restaurant. Gatsby vanishes after Nick introduces him to Tom. What's all that

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:55.749
about? Later that afternoon, Jordan gives Nick the scoop. 5 years ago back in

00:04:55.759 --> 00:05:03.110
Louisville, Daisy had a steamy love affair with a young army officer named Jay Gatsby.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:11.830
But then Gatsby went off to war and Daisy married Tom Buchanan. Gatsby has been pining for Daisy ever since. He

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:19.909
even bought that crazy mansion to be close to her. He throws big parties in the hope that Daisy will show up to one,

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:24.310
but she hasn't. So now it's down to Nick.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:33.990
Gatsby wants Nick to invite Daisy to afternoon tea at his cottage, but Daisy isn't to know that Gatsby will be there.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:42.469
Being a beautiful friend, Nick invites Daisy over a few days later. Gatsby shows up an hour earlier, looking

00:05:42.479 --> 00:05:50.629
sleepdeprived. When Daisy arrives, Gatsby runs out through the back door and knocks on the front door as if he's just arrived,

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:54.790
fashionably late. Cool moves, old sport.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:04.550
The lover's reunion is super awkward at first. Daisy hardly knows what to say, but eventually the atmosphere shifts

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:13.029
until Daisy and Gatsby are absolutely absorbed in one another. Gatsby then takes Daisy and Nick next door for a

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:21.590
tour of his jaw-dropping house. Goodness knows how he earned the money to buy it in only 3 years. As the evening draws

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:24.870
in, Nick decides to leave them to it.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:28.230
They don't need him anymore.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:37.670
After this, Nick doesn't see Gatsby for a few weeks, so he uses this interval to tell us more about the Great Gatsby. Jay

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:46.309
Gatsby was born James Gats, the son of poor farmers from the Midwest. But Gatsby had big dreams and reinvented

00:06:46.319 --> 00:06:57.990
himself at age 17. His career officially began when he introduced himself as Jay Gatsby to the millionaire Dan Cody. Cody

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:05.909
became Gatsby's employer and mentor, teaching him how to be a man of substance.

00:07:05.919 --> 00:07:09.270
Nick visits Gatsby one Sunday afternoon.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:18.390
Tom Buchanan and his posh riding buddies also drop in as if Gatsby's house is a pub. The way these East Egg toss treat

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:27.350
Gatsby is quite rude. Although Gatsby makes a point of telling Tom, "I know your wife." Sure enough, Tom and Daisy

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:36.950
show up to Gatsby's next party. Except Daisy doesn't enjoy herself. West Egg just isn't her scene. At the end of the

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:45.350
night, Tom announces that he's going to find out who Gatsby really is. Uh-oh.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:53.909
A short time later, Nick, Jordan, and Gatsby are invited to the Buchanan for lunch. It's not long before Tom sniffs

00:07:53.919 --> 00:08:03.909
out the affair. Instead of exploding then and there, he decides they'll all go into the city, so Tom drives Nick and

00:08:03.919 --> 00:08:13.589
Jordan in Gatsby's car, while Gatsby drives Daisy in Tom's blue coupé. On the way, Tom stops by Wilson's garage for

00:08:13.599 --> 00:08:23.510
gas. While George fills Gatsby's car, he tells Tom that he and Myrtle are leaving town for good. Nick sees Myrtle staring

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:32.630
down at the car from an upstairs window. Will Tom lose his wife and mistress on the same day.

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:40.790
After they reach the Plaza Hotel, Tom confronts Gatsby about his affair with Daisy. Gatsby rises to the challenge,

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:49.829
but Tom quickly gains the upper hand. When Daisy loses the nerve to end her marriage, Tom goes for the jugular. He

00:08:49.839 --> 00:08:57.990
reveals how Gatsby makes his millions from organized crime with Meyer Wolfsheim. Gatsby tries to deny it, but

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.389
Daisy shuts down. She wants to go home.

00:09:02.399 --> 00:09:11.269
Tom's so sure of his victory that he tells Gatsby to take Daisy home in his own car this time. When Myrtle Wilson

00:09:11.279 --> 00:09:16.790
sees Gatsby's big yellow car coming, she runs out onto the road to flag it down.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:23.509
But the car doesn't stop. It hits Myrtle, killing her instantly.

00:09:23.519 --> 00:09:32.230
By the time Tom pulls up at Wilson's garage, a crowd has gathered. Tom soon realizes what's happened. A policeman is

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:40.470
recording details about a big yellow car. So Tom acts quickly. He grabs George, sits him down, and denies any

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:49.829
personal connection to the car. On the drive home, Tom sobs quietly, blaming Gatsby for Myrtle's death. But by the

00:09:49.839 --> 00:09:55.269
time they reach Tom's house, he's pulled himself together.

00:09:55.279 --> 00:10:03.910
As Nick waits for his taxi, Gatsby emerges from the bushes. Nick tells Gatsby that the woman he hit on the road

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:13.350
was killed. Gatsby admits that Daisy was driving, but he'll say he was driving if anyone asks. For now, he's waiting in

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:19.269
the garden in case Tom hassles Daisy about the ugly scene at the Plaza Hotel.

00:10:19.279 --> 00:10:28.389
Nick is suddenly concerned. What if Tom finds out that Daisy killed Myrtle? Nick peers through a window to check on them,

00:10:28.399 --> 00:10:36.630
but all he sees is Tom and Daisy talking. They look united, almost as if they're conspiring.

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:46.710
Nick assures Gatsby that Daisy is fine, but Gatsby stays just in case. Gatsby returns home at dawn, having waited for

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:56.470
nothing. Nick goes to see Gatsby and tells him to leave town for a while. But Gatsby wants to stay until he knows what Daisy wants

00:10:56.480 --> 00:11:05.190
to do. Meanwhile, George Wilson is on a mission to find the owner of the big yellow car.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:14.150
Deranged with grief and lack of sleep, he'd started walking towards West Egg just after dawn. At some point on his

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:22.550
journey, someone gives him Gatsby's name. He reaches Gatsby's house at around 300 p.m. and finds Gatsby in his

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:32.230
pool. Sensing trouble, Nick rushes to Gatsby's house after work, but he's too late. He finds Gatsby lying dead on his

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:40.389
inflatable pool mattress. George Wilson's body is sprawled in the grass nearby.

00:11:40.399 --> 00:11:48.550
When no one comes forward to handle Gatsby's affairs, Nick becomes Gatsby's champion. It seems that no one else

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:58.550
cares. With radio silence from Daisy and a cowardly refusal from Meyer Wolfsheim, Nick is disgusted with everyone.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:07.110
But then Gatsby's father shows up. Henry C. Gats left Minnesota as soon as he read about his son's death in the

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:17.910
newspaper. Even though Gatsby or Jimmy had walked out on his parents many years prior, Henry was still very proud of his son.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:24.470
Once he became successful, Gatsby was generous with his parents.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:34.310
Only one more unexpected person attends Gatsby's funeral. The Allied man from Gatsby's library. of Gatsby's legions of

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:40.470
guests, Allies is the only one who pays his respects.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:46.949
Soon after this, Nick decides to return home to the Midwest.

00:12:46.959 --> 00:12:54.949
When he meets Jordan Baker to break things off, she coolly informs him that she's already engaged to someone else.

00:12:54.959 --> 00:13:04.870
Ouch. A short time later, Nick encounters Tom Buchanan on the street. Nick refuses to shake his hand. He assumes Tom was the

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:14.629
one who gave Gatsby's name to George Wilson. Tom admits that he did, but he'd basically done it at gunpoint. Besides,

00:13:14.639 --> 00:13:22.710
Tom believed Gatsby deserved it for being a liar and for killing Myrtle like a stray dog. It seems that Daisy hasn't

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:30.470
admitted to being the driver. What a bunch of rotten, careless snobs.

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:36.550
On Nick's last night, he sits on Gatsby's beach, gazing across the bay.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:45.269
He imagines how hopeful Gatsby must have felt when he saw that green light at the end of Daisy's dock. But Gatsby failed

00:13:45.279 --> 00:13:52.389
to realize that his dream of a life with Daisy belonged to the past. It was over.

00:13:52.399 --> 00:14:01.829
Perhaps we all have a touch of Gatsby in us with our relentless pursuit of dreams and bright futures, but to Nick, we're

00:14:01.839 --> 00:14:08.470
more like boats beating against a current that pulls us back.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:17.350
Gatsby's beautiful dream crumbled into a delusion and ended as a nightmare. His epic failure might be a lesson for all

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:27.350
of us. Then again, maybe we could all just dream big, work hard, and avoid rotten crowds like the Buchanan.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:34.389
What do you think?

00:14:34.399 --> 00:14:39.430
We hope you enjoyed this schooling online production.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:45.399
For more easy lessons, check out our other videos.
